from (values
('127.410.d.10.D',4,'A slender bar in compression can fail by sideways bending called:','["buckling", "tension", "melting", "polishing"]'::jsonb,0,'Buckling limits compression members.','original'),
('127.410.d.10.E',3,'A zero-force member in a truss is one that carries:','["all the weight", "no load under the given loading", "extra paint", "maximum load"]'::jsonb,1,'Some members carry no force in certain loadings.','original'),
('127.410.d.10.E',4,'Members in a loaded truss may be in tension or compression depending on the:','["color of the truss", "name of the engineer", "direction of the loads", "time of day"]'::jsonb,2,'Load direction determines the member state.','original'),
('127.410.d.10.F',3,'A tensegrity structure is held in shape by a balance of continuous tension and isolated:','["shadows", "magnets", "bubbles", "compression members"]'::jsonb,3,'Struts float within a tension network.','original'),
('127.410.d.10.F',4,'Bridge trusses often use triangles because triangles make the structure:','["rigid with efficient use of material", "floppy", "colorful", "heavy only"]'::jsonb,0,'Triangles resist shape change.','original'),
('127.410.d.11.A',3,'A two-dimensional structure analysis assumes all forces and members lie in one:','["room", "plane", "color", "season"]'::jsonb,1,'2D means flat analysis.','original'),
('127.410.d.11.A',4,'A three-dimensional analysis needs equilibrium equations in x, y, and:','["q", "t only", "z", "w"]'::jsonb,2,'3D adds the third axis.','original'),
('127.410.d.11.B',3,'Adding a third dimension to a structure generally increases the number of:','["words", "labels only", "colors", "equations and unknowns"]'::jsonb,3,'Six equilibrium equations replace three.','original'),
('127.410.d.11.B',4,'In three dimensions, the number of equilibrium equations for a rigid body is:','["six", "nine", "three", "two"]'::jsonb,0,'Three force and three moment equations.','original'),
('127.410.d.11.C',3,'A flat frame that is stable in its own plane can still fall over sideways if it has no:','["name", "out-of-plane bracing", "paint", "label"]'::jsonb,1,'Sideways bracing supplies 3D stability.','original'),
('127.410.d.11.C',4,'A tall sign supported by one planar truss can be unstable against wind from the side unless a second plane of members is:','["hidden", "removed", "added", "painted"]'::jsonb,2,'Bracing in the second plane gives stability.','original'),
('127.411.d.1',3,'An engineering team finds that a cheaper part may fail early. The professional choice is to:','["ship it quickly", "hide the risk", "blame the customer", "report the risk and fix the design"]'::jsonb,3,'Safety and honesty come before cost savings.','original'),
('127.411.d.1',4,'Safe lab practice when using power tools includes wearing:','["eye protection", "open sandals", "earbuds only", "loose sleeves"]'::jsonb,0,'Protective gear prevents injuries.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.A',3,'The first stage of the engineering design process is to define the:','["price", "problem", "logo", "color"]'::jsonb,1,'Design starts with a clear problem statement.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.A',4,'A good problem statement describes the need, the users, and the:','["team mascot", "weather forecast", "constraints", "paint brand"]'::jsonb,2,'Constraints bound the solution.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.B',3,'Gathering information about similar products and user needs is called:','["guessing", "shipping", "painting", "research"]'::jsonb,3,'Research informs the design.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.B',4,'Which source would help a team learn how customers use a product?','["a user survey", "a color wheel", "a random coin flip", "a clock"]'::jsonb,0,'Surveys collect user needs.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.C',3,'Brainstorming many possible solutions without judging them is called:','["inspection", "ideation", "shipping", "accounting"]'::jsonb,1,'Ideation generates options.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.C',4,'During ideation, the team should aim for a large number of:','["identical ideas", "deadlines", "different ideas", "criticisms"]'::jsonb,2,'Quantity and variety spark good concepts.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.D',3,'A tool that scores design options against weighted criteria is a:','["tape measure", "rubber band", "paint chart", "decision matrix"]'::jsonb,3,'A matrix compares concepts objectively.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.D',4,'In a decision matrix, the option with the highest weighted total is usually:','["selected for development", "painted", "hidden", "discarded"]'::jsonb,0,'The best-scoring concept moves forward.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.E',3,'A scale drawing that shows the exact shape and size of a part is a:','["poster", "technical drawing", "diary", "cartoon"]'::jsonb,1,'Technical drawings communicate dimensions.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.E',4,'A quick physical model made of cardboard to test a concept is a:','["invoice", "final product", "prototype", "logo"]'::jsonb,2,'Prototypes test ideas cheaply.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.F',3,'A fair test changes only one variable at a time so the team can tell what caused the:','["lunch", "weather", "music", "result"]'::jsonb,3,'Single-variable tests isolate cause.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.F',4,'Testing the prototype under realistic load is part of:','["experimental design and testing", "advertising", "payroll", "packaging"]'::jsonb,0,'Tests show whether the design performs.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.G',3,'Repeating design steps to improve a solution based on test results is called:','["storage", "iteration", "retirement", "subtraction"]'::jsonb,1,'Iteration refines the design.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.G',4,'After a prototype fails a test, the team should:','["hide the data", "blame the tester", "analyze why and revise the design", "stop forever"]'::jsonb,2,'Failures guide improvements.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.H',3,'Sharing the final design with others through reports and presentations is the step of:','["hiding", "deletion", "demolition", "communication"]'::jsonb,3,'The team documents and presents results.','original'),
('127.411.d.2.H',4,'A design presentation should include the problem, the solution, and the:','["test evidence", "team playlist", "lunch menu", "paint sample"]'::jsonb,0,'Evidence supports the solution.','original'),
('127.411.d.3.A',3,'A team has 10 days to build a model. A good time management step is to make a:','["random plan", "schedule with due dates", "nap plan", "longer lunch"]'::jsonb,1,'Schedules keep work on track.','original'),
('127.411.d.3.A',4,'Doing the hardest or longest tasks first helps a team avoid:','["early starts", "planning", "last-minute delays", "good grades"]'::jsonb,2,'Early progress reduces risk.','original'),
('127.411.d.3.B',3,'A limit on money, time, or materials in a project is a:','["color", "bonus", "feature", "constraint"]'::jsonb,3,'Constraints restrict choices.','original'),
('127.411.d.3.B',4,'A project has a fixed budget of 50 dollars. That budget is a:','["cost constraint", "size goal", "color preference", "time constraint"]'::jsonb,0,'Budget limits spending.','original'),
('127.411.d.3.C',3,'A milestone in a project is a:','["logo", "key checkpoint", "lunch break", "mistake"]'::jsonb,1,'Milestones mark progress points.','original'),
('127.411.d.3.D',3,'Which is a written form of communication on a team?','["a hand wave", "a whistle", "an email or report", "a nod"]'::jsonb,2,'Written communication leaves a record.','original'),
('127.411.d.3.D',4,'A team uses a shared document so everyone sees the same:','["blank pages", "old drafts only", "private notes only", "current information"]'::jsonb,3,'Shared documents keep teams aligned.','original'),
('127.411.d.3.E',3,'When a team is stuck, a useful problem-solving strategy is to break the problem into:','["smaller parts", "bigger problems", "fewer facts", "bad ideas"]'::jsonb,0,'Decomposition makes problems manageable.','original'),
('127.411.d.3.E',4,'Working backward from the goal to the first step is a strategy called:','["random guessing", "backward planning", "stalling", "skipping"]'::jsonb,1,'Backward planning clarifies steps.','original'),
('127.411.d.4.A',3,'Helpful critique of a teammate''s idea should focus on the:','["person, not the work", "noise", "work, not the person", "teammate''s looks"]'::jsonb,2,'Constructive critique targets the idea.','original'),
('127.411.d.4.A',4,'A respectful critique includes a specific suggestion for:','["who to blame", "what to hide", "why the person is bad", "how to improve"]'::jsonb,3,'Specific advice helps.','original'),
('127.411.d.4.B',3,'A teammate who listens, shares tasks fairly, and meets deadlines shows good:','["teamwork skills", "spelling", "sleep habits", "solo habits"]'::jsonb,0,'Reliable cooperation helps teams.','original'),
('127.411.d.4.B',4,'If two teammates disagree, a good first step is to:','["shout", "listen to each side", "ignore both", "quit"]'::jsonb,1,'Understanding both views leads to solutions.','original'),
('127.411.d.4.C',3,'A bar chart that shows tasks over time with start and end dates is a:','["map", "pie chart", "Gantt chart", "line graph of weather"]'::jsonb,2,'Gantt charts schedule tasks.','original'),
('127.411.d.4.C',4,'A work breakdown structure divides a project into smaller:','["rooms", "voices", "colors", "tasks"]'::jsonb,3,'It lists the work in pieces.','original'),
('127.411.d.4.D',3,'A team member contributes positively by completing assigned tasks:','["on time and with quality", "late", "partly", "never"]'::jsonb,0,'Reliable work supports the team.','original'),
('127.411.d.4.D',4,'Offering to help a teammate who is behind shows:','["poor planning", "positive group contribution", "bad manners", "cheating"]'::jsonb,1,'Helping improves team results.','original'),
('127.411.d.5.A',3,'A short summary at the start of a report that gives the main findings is an:','["index card", "footnote", "executive summary", "appendix"]'::jsonb,2,'It gives busy readers the key points.','original'),
('127.411.d.5.A',4,'A reverse engineering report documents how an existing product is:','["advertised", "named", "sold", "built and how it works"]'::jsonb,3,'It records the analysis of a product.','original'),
('127.411.d.5.B',3,'Technical reports usually include headings so readers can find:','["sections quickly", "only pictures", "only colors", "nothing"]'::jsonb,0,'Format aids navigation.','original'),
('127.411.d.5.B',4,'A report uses figures and captions to help explain:','["weather", "data and designs", "lunch", "jokes"]'::jsonb,1,'Visuals support understanding.','original'),
('127.411.d.5.C',3,'A well-organized report presents the introduction, then the body, then the:','["blank page", "title again", "conclusion", "lunch"]'::jsonb,2,'Logical order helps the reader.','original'),
('127.411.d.5.C',4,'Steps in a procedure should be listed in the:','["order of difficulty", "random order", "alphabetical order", "order they are done"]'::jsonb,3,'Sequence must match the real process.','original'),
('127.411.d.6.A',3,'Mechanical design is used to make products such as cars, bicycles, and:','["washing machines", "clouds", "poems", "songs"]'::jsonb,0,'Many machines are mechanically designed.','original'),
('127.411.d.6.A',4,'A company that makes engines and gearboxes is in the field of:','["poetry", "mechanical design and manufacturing", "music publishing", "fashion only"]'::jsonb,1,'These parts require mechanical engineering.','original'),
('127.411.d.6.B',3,'A commercial use of mechanical design is the production of:','["lullabies", "dreams", "elevators", "stories"]'::jsonb,2,'Elevators use mechanisms and structures.','original')
