('127.411.d.6.B',4,'Wind turbines, cranes, and pumps are examples of products with:','["no moving parts", "only graphic design", "no materials", "mechanical design"]'::jsonb,3,'Each has designed mechanisms.','original'),
('127.411.d.6.C',3,'A household item with a designed mechanism is a:','["can opener", "blanket", "pillow", "rug"]'::jsonb,0,'Can openers use gears and levers.','original'),
('127.411.d.6.C',4,'A door lock uses a mechanism to convert a key turn into:','["heat", "bolt movement", "light", "sound only"]'::jsonb,1,'The lock moves the bolt.','original'),
('127.411.d.7.A',3,'A computer model that shows how parts of a machine move together is a:','["receipt", "poster", "virtual model of a mechanism", "paper plane"]'::jsonb,2,'Virtual models simulate motion.','original'),
('127.411.d.7.A',4,'An advantage of testing a mechanism in a virtual model first is that the team can find problems:','["after selling it", "by luck", "never", "before building it"]'::jsonb,3,'Simulation saves time and material.','original'),
