('127.411.d.7.D',3,'Changing a gear''s number of teeth in a model changes the mechanism''s:','["speed ratio", "price tag", "label", "color"]'::jsonb,0,'Tooth count sets the ratio.','original'),
('127.411.d.7.D',4,'Making a lever arm longer in the model changes the force and the:','["paint", "distance moved", "brand", "font"]'::jsonb,1,'Lever geometry trades force for distance.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.A',3,'Before taking a product apart for reverse engineering, you should gather the correct:','["toys", "paints", "tools", "songs"]'::jsonb,2,'The right tools prevent damage.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.A',4,'While disassembling a product, a good habit is to photograph and label each:','["window", "table leg", "cloud", "removed part"]'::jsonb,3,'Documentation helps reassembly.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.B',3,'Keeping notes, sketches, and photos while taking something apart is called:','["documentation", "decoration", "distraction", "deletion"]'::jsonb,0,'Records capture the product''s design.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.B',4,'A bill of materials lists each part and its:','["rumor", "quantity", "favorite color", "nickname"]'::jsonb,1,'A BOM records what is in the assembly.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.C',3,'The part that transfers motor power to the wheels in a toy car is part of the:','["label", "manual", "drive system", "packaging"]'::jsonb,2,'Drive systems carry power.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.C',4,'Counting teeth on two meshing gears lets you compute the:','["color", "weight of the box", "price", "gear ratio"]'::jsonb,3,'Ratio = teeth driven / teeth driver.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.D',3,'A housing or cover on a product mainly serves to protect internal parts and provide:','["a shape for the user", "extra weight only", "noise", "no function"]'::jsonb,0,'Covers protect and shape the product.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.D',4,'Switches and buttons on a device are its:','["fasteners", "controls", "housings", "gears"]'::jsonb,1,'Controls let the user operate it.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.E',3,'A caliper is used to measure the:','["speed of sound", "color", "dimensions of a part", "temperature"]'::jsonb,2,'Calipers measure small lengths precisely.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.E',4,'Measuring a part three times and averaging helps reduce:','["cost of tools", "part weight", "paint use", "measurement error"]'::jsonb,3,'Repeated measurement improves accuracy.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.F',3,'Magnet tests, hardness tests, and visual inspection help identify a part''s:','["material", "price tag", "shipping address", "owner"]'::jsonb,0,'Simple tests suggest the material.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.F',4,'A part that is attracted to a magnet is likely made of:','["aluminum", "iron or steel", "copper", "plastic"]'::jsonb,1,'Ferrous metals are magnetic.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.G',3,'Seams and ejector pin marks on a plastic part suggest it was made by:','["hand carving", "knitting", "injection molding", "weaving"]'::jsonb,2,'Molding leaves characteristic marks.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.G',4,'A part with a rough, grainy surface and a visible parting line was probably produced by:','["drawing", "printing", "sewing", "casting"]'::jsonb,3,'Casting leaves seams and texture.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.H',3,'Observing the order in which parts are removed helps you understand the product''s:','["assembly process", "resale price", "shipping route", "advertising"]'::jsonb,0,'Reverse order reveals how it was assembled.','original'),
('127.411.d.8.H',4,'Screws, clips, and adhesives found during disassembly are called:','["covers", "fasteners", "controls", "gears"]'::jsonb,1,'Fasteners hold parts together.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.A',3,'Stamping makes a part by pressing sheet metal in a:','["bucket", "blender", "die", "drawer"]'::jsonb,2,'A die shapes the metal.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.A',4,'A car door panel is commonly formed from sheet steel by:','["knitting", "sintering", "casting", "stamping"]'::jsonb,3,'Large panels are stamped.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.B',3,'In injection molding, plastic pellets are loaded into a hopper and melted by a:','["heater", "fan", "magnet", "freezer"]'::jsonb,0,'The barrel heats the plastic.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.B',4,'After melted plastic is injected into a mold, the part must be allowed to:','["evaporate", "cool and harden", "freeze the machine", "boil"]'::jsonb,1,'Cooling sets the shape.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.C',3,'In casting, a furnace melts metal that is then poured into a:','["sink", "vending machine", "mold", "bucket of paint"]'::jsonb,2,'The mold gives the shape.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.C',4,'A cavity shaped like the desired part is used in:','["drawing", "painting walls", "knitting", "casting and molding"]'::jsonb,3,'Both use a shaped cavity.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.D',3,'Sintering forms solid parts by heating compacted metal powder below its:','["melting point", "boiling point of water", "shadow", "freezing point"]'::jsonb,0,'Particles bond without fully melting.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.D',4,'A porous metal bearing may be made by sintering because the process leaves tiny:','["colors", "pores", "wires", "screws"]'::jsonb,1,'Pores can hold lubricant.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.E',3,'Drilling, milling, and turning are examples of:','["molding", "stamping", "material removal", "casting"]'::jsonb,2,'They cut material away.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.E',4,'A lathe produces round parts by spinning the workpiece against a:','["mold", "paintbrush", "magnet", "cutting tool"]'::jsonb,3,'Turning removes material.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.F',3,'A jig or fixture holds a workpiece in place during:','["manufacturing or assembly", "lunch", "sleep", "music"]'::jsonb,0,'Fixtures keep parts positioned.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.F',4,'Using a fixture so every part is positioned the same way improves:','["noise", "repeatability", "rust", "confusion"]'::jsonb,1,'Consistent positions give consistent parts.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.G',3,'A material well suited to casting because it melts easily is:','["rubber band", "wood", "aluminum", "glass fiber cloth"]'::jsonb,2,'Aluminum casts well.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.G',4,'Sheet steel is a suitable material for stamping because it can be:','["blown like glass", "dissolved in water", "burned", "formed without cracking"]'::jsonb,3,'Ductile sheet forms well.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.H',3,'Choosing a manufacturing process depends on the part''s shape, material, and the number to be:','["produced", "hidden", "admired", "renamed"]'::jsonb,0,'Quantity affects process choice.','original'),
('127.411.d.9.H',4,'Making millions of identical plastic parts at low cost per part usually favors:','["sculpting", "injection molding", "one-off machining", "hand carving"]'::jsonb,1,'Molds pay off at high volume.','original'),
('127.411.d.10.A',3,'Joining two metal parts by melting them together at the joint is called:','["gluing", "taping", "welding", "stapling"]'::jsonb,2,'Welding fuses the metals.','original'),
('127.411.d.10.A',4,'Joining two plastic or wood parts with a chemical that cures between them is:','["welding with an arc", "stamping", "casting", "adhesive bonding"]'::jsonb,3,'Adhesives bond surfaces.','original'),
('127.411.d.10.B',3,'A joining method that can be taken apart later without damage is a:','["bolted joint", "glued joint", "welded joint", "brazed joint"]'::jsonb,0,'Bolts can be removed.','original'),
('127.411.d.10.B',4,'An engineer choosing between welding and screws should weigh strength, cost, and whether the joint must be:','["painted blue", "disassembled", "admired", "named"]'::jsonb,1,'Serviceability matters.','original'),
('127.411.d.10.C',3,'Planning the order in which parts are put together is an:','["advertising plan", "music plan", "assembly strategy", "lunch plan"]'::jsonb,2,'Assembly order affects cost and quality.','original'),
('127.411.d.10.C',4,'Designing parts so they can only be installed one correct way helps prevent:','["good sales", "strong parts", "low cost", "assembly errors"]'::jsonb,3,'Error-proofing reduces mistakes.','original'),
('127.411.d.11.A',3,'FMEA stands for failure modes and effects:','["analysis", "adjustment", "assembly", "agreement"]'::jsonb,0,'It studies how things can fail.','original'),
('127.411.d.11.A',4,'In FMEA, a failure mode is a way in which a part could:','["be painted", "fail to work", "be named", "be sold"]'::jsonb,1,'Failure modes describe how failure happens.','original'),
('127.411.d.11.B',3,'Quality function deployment, or QFD, helps teams connect customer needs to:','["team songs", "lunch menus", "engineering requirements", "dress codes"]'::jsonb,2,'QFD translates voice of customer.','original'),
